export const PRIVACY_MD = "# Thinnava Privacy Policy\n\n_Last updated: 19 October 2026. Contact: distilledwater.ck@gmail.com_\n\nThinnava (\"Thinnava\", \"we\") is a student project built at the Indian Institute of Science (IISc). It helps you remember where you and the people you know have eaten. This policy explains what we collect and why, in plain words.\n\n## What we collect\n- **From your Google account, when you sign in:** your name, email address and profile photo. We use them to create your account. We never see your Google password.\n- **What you create in the app:** your profile (name, username, bio), your visits and reviews, the places on your wishlist, what friends told you that you saved, internet finds and their links, your connections, your lists, and who you tagged.\n- **Your location:** only when you allow it, and only while you use the app, to centre the map and show nearby places first. We don't store your location.\n- **A notification token:** if you turn on notifications, so we can send you requests and tags.\n\n## Who can see what\n- People you're **not connected** with see only your name, username and photo.\n- **Connections** see the visits and wishlist you share with them, based on the lists you choose (\"All connections\", \"Only me\", or your own lists).\n- What you log about a friend's experience, and internet finds, are **only ever visible to you**.\n\n## Shared messages and AI\nWhen you share a message or link into Thinnava, its text is sent to **Google's Gemini** service to pick out the place, dishes and price. You check everything before saving. **Thinnava does not store the original message.** For internet finds, the link you shared is saved with your entry. Google may process the text under its own terms.\n\n## Place information\nPlace names, addresses and locations come from **Ola Maps** and **OpenStreetMap** (© OpenStreetMap contributors). When you search for a place, what you type is sent to Ola Maps from our server, not from your phone. Place names picked out of a shared message are looked up on OpenStreetMap. Opening hours and contact details are only fetched when you ask for them. The map on the website is drawn by **OpenFreeMap**, which sees the area of the map you're looking at, like any map website. If you add a place yourself, its name and area can be found by everyone on Thinnava.\n\n## What we don't do\nNo ads. We don't sell or share your data with anyone for marketing. No tracking or analytics.\n\n## Where data is stored\nYour data is stored with **Supabase**, our database provider, in its Mumbai (India) region.\n\n## Deleting your data\nYou can delete your account at any time from **Settings → Delete account**. This permanently deletes everything you created. Your name is removed from other people's tags.\n\n## Changes\nIf this policy changes, we'll update this page and the date above.\n\n## Contact\nQuestions: distilledwater.ck@gmail.com";
export const TERMS_MD = "# Thinnava Terms of Use\n\n_Last updated: 19 October 2026. Contact: distilledwater.ck@gmail.com_\n\n1. **What this is.** Thinnava is a student project from IISc, offered free and \"as is\", with no guarantees that it will always be available or error-free.\n2. **Your account.** You sign in with Google. Keep your account to yourself, and give a real name and a username that isn't offensive or impersonating someone.\n3. **Be respectful.** Don't post anything illegal, hateful, harassing, or anything that shares someone else's private information. Reviews are your own honest opinions.\n4. **Your content.** What you post stays yours. You allow us to store and show it to the people you choose, so the app can work.\n5. **Third-party services.** Place information comes from Ola Maps and OpenStreetMap, directions open Google Maps, and order buttons open Swiggy. Those services have their own terms. Places you add yourself must be real food places; don't add anything misleading.\n6. **Removal.** We may remove content or accounts that break these terms.\n7. **Changes.** We may update these terms. Continuing to use the app means you accept the updated terms.\n8. **Contact:** distilledwater.ck@gmail.com";
